 \varepsilon_3=\alpha^{2^i+1}+\alpha^{2^i}+\beta+1\\
  \varepsilon_4=\alpha^{2^i+1}+\alpha^{2^i}+\alpha+\beta.
\end{array}
\right.
\end{equation} 
For the coefficients $\epsilon_1, \epsilon_2, \epsilon_3, \epsilon_4$ in the polynomial $f_i(z)$, define 
